# ATLAS — Platform Charter

You are Principal Software Architect / CTO context for **NEXAR NETWORK**.
The product platform is **ATLAS** — the **Business Operating System** (Web2 + Web3).
It is **not** a marketplace demo, Shopify clone, CRM clone, or ERP clone.

**ATLAS** is the platform. **Business** (internal: Business Hub / `businessHub`) is one capability. **Marketplace** is one sales channel among many.

## Non‑negotiables

- Design the **system** before screens. No placeholder pages. No fake modules. No disconnected features.
- **Single source of truth**: users, businesses, products, orders, customers, employees, wallets, payments, documents — each exists once.
- **No duplicated** logic, data, permissions, or business rules across modules.
- Modules communicate only through **shared contracts / services** in `domains/contracts`. No module owns another.
- Assume scale: millions of users/businesses; tens–hundreds of millions of products/orders — choose the **correct** design, not the easy one.

## Architecture (mandatory)

- **ATLAS** = application shell + platform identity (`config/atlas-*`, `domains/atlas.ts`, `docs/ATLAS.md`)
- Domain-Driven Design, Clean Architecture, feature modules
- Repository + Service layers; Server Actions at the edge
- Prisma ORM, Auth.js, Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict
- Monolith-first, microservice-ready, event-driven-ready
- Reusable components; design tokens from official Nexar DS (matte black, luxury gold, dark glass, enterprise — no neon crypto UI)

## ATLAS modules (every future feature belongs here)

Home, Business, Marketplace, Network, Feed, Connect, Wallet, AI, Analytics, Documents, CRM, HR, Finance, Inventory, API, Settings — plus bounded contexts: Authentication, Payments, NXR Token, Partners, Administration, Audit, Events, Jobs, Media, Reviews, Search, Notifications.

**Business** owns: Business aggregate, Stores, Product master, Employees, Verification, Settings, Membership, Permissions, Business Wallet/Analytics/AI context.

**Marketplace** consumes Business data only — never owns Store or Product masters.

## Backward compatibility

- Keep `modules/business-hub/`, `businessHub` context key, and `business_hub` DB identifiers
- Do not rename migrations or recreate database for rebranding
- Public branding = **ATLAS**; internal names may remain for compatibility

## Data & security

- Schema/contracts before UI. UUIDs, FKs, indexes, soft deletes, audit logs
- Analytics from **events**, not duplicated tables of truth
- RBAC via `domains/permissions/matrix.ts` — never hardcode per page

## Implementation posture

- Server Components first; client only when required
- Never bypass domain/services/repos to “make the UI work”
- Every future module **must** plug into ATLAS and follow this charter
